# EVERYTHING in this directory is consumed by Linux tools inside WSL: bash runs
# the scripts, arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc compiles the C, python3 runs the rest.
# The repo root already pins *.sh, but the C here is full of multi-line macros
# with backslash continuations, which is precisely the shape a stray CR ruins —
# the same failure the root .gitattributes records for Dockerfiles. Pin the lot
# rather than reason about which file survives CRLF.
* text eol=lf

# Never touch the run artefacts, on the off-chance one is ever force-added.
*.png binary
*.raw binary
# The windows' icons (icons/, installer/make_rig_icons.py) are committed and
# shipped. Under `* text` the first playfield.ico WAS committed with the CR of
# its ten CR LF pairs taken out - a truncated icon that pywebview then fails to
# load - so every binary format in icons/ is named here.
*.ico binary
*.argb binary

# The Mode SDK's PINNED runtime object (item 127, modes/sdk/prebuilt/mode.so) is
# committed and shipped. Its rule MUST be here: a deeper .gitattributes wins, so the
# root file's `binary` line lost to `* text eol=lf` above, and a rebuild whose bytes
# held a CR LF pair would have been committed with the CR taken out.
*.so binary
